# Palm - hand drums.
#
# Each note is a head tuned to the note: the modes of a circular membrane,
# or a tabla's, tuned to a harmonic series by the paste in its middle. The
# hand does the rest. `stroke` picks open, slap, muted, bass or rim, or lets
# the velocity choose (soft is muted, hard is slapped); `position` moves it
# towards the middle or the edge, `hand` makes it softer or quicker, and
# `damp` rests the other hand on the head.
#
# A djembe's goblet and a cajón's box ring low under a bass stroke (`body`);
# `rattle` is a cajón's snares, a djembe's rattles or a frame drum's
# jingles. A head struck hard goes sharp and settles (`drop`); pressure or
# the mod wheel squeezes a bayan or a talking drum up by `squeeze`
# semitones. Slide (with MPE) lays a finger on the head. `roll` strikes held
# notes again and again.
#
# `flam` makes each hit two strokes, a softer grace stroke and then the
# stroke this many milliseconds later.
#
# Kit mode makes the sixteen keys from note 36 up into pads, each with its
# own drum, stroke, note and level.
#
# A hundred and twelve patches in six families, plainest first:
#
#   africa   Init, djembes, talking drums, ashiko and udu (22)
#   latin    cajón, congas, bongos, batá and cuíca (24)
#   arabic   frame drums, darbuka, riq, tar and bendir (23)
#   india    tabla, bayan, kanjira, mridangam and dholak (23)
#   kit      sixteen pads: world, cajón, frame, congas, tabla, talking, udu
#            (12)
#   odd      heads far out of range, talking drum and udu basses, a squeeze
#            an octave wide (8)
#
# Each family ends with its flams, the patches played by touch, and rolls.
# A "By Touch" patch lets the velocity pick the stroke. Talking By Touch,
# Bayan Press and Squeeze Sweep are played with pressure or the mod wheel,
# and the harness plays them in a gallop with the wheel moving.
#
# Values are in each parameter's own units; `audition params Palm` lists
# them. A patch names only what it changes. Every patch sits near -30 on
# `loud` at its own note, from -34.5 (Conga Muted) to -25.8 (Frame Roll):
# muted and edge strokes are the quiet end, rolls the loud. Every kit peaks
# at about -5 dB on its loudest pad.
#
# Every patch but Init carries eight named macros. Destinations are
# numbered as in Palm.h's MacroDest: #1 position, #2 hand, #3 decay, #4 damp,
# #5 drop, #7 rattle, #8 body, #9 roll, #10 spread, #12 volume, #13 flam,
# #14 pitch (24 semitones a unit). Most patches have Middle (Edge on a bass
# stroke), Quick, Ring, Damp, one that fits the drum (Body or Dry on a bass
# stroke; Rattles, Snares or Jingles, or Bare where they are already on;
# Drop otherwise), Flam, Roll and Tight. The cuíca has Low, Wide and High in
# place of what does nothing on it, the udu Drop and Low. Kits have Edge,
# Quick, Ring, Damp, Body or Tight, Jingles, Bare or Drop, Flam, and Wide or
# Roll. A kit's macros reach the drum params every pad shares, never a pad's
# own drum, stroke, note or level. Where a macro at full moves the level by
# more than 1.5 dB, a volume route takes it back out, as far as the volume
# knob goes; Damp is gentler where the volume is near the top. Position,
# hand, decay, damp, drop, body and flam are read when a drum is struck, so
# those macros change the next hit.

machine Palm
role tune

# --- africa ------------------------------------------------------------------

patch Init family=africa note=55 range=45..67

patch "Djembe Bass" family=africa note=55 range=45..67 role=bass
  # The palm in the middle: the goblet's air booms under it.
  set macro1 "Edge"
  set macro2 "Quick"
  set macro3 "Ring"
  set macro4 "Damp"
  set macro5 "Dry"
  set macro6 "Flam"
  set macro7 "Roll"
  set macro8 "Tight"
  mac1_d1  #1
  mac1_a1  0.5
  mac1_d2  #12
  mac1_a2  0.3
  mac2_d1  #2
  mac2_a1  0.4
  mac3_d1  #3
  mac3_a1  0.35
  mac3_d2  #12
  mac3_a2  -0.157
  mac4_d1  #4
  mac4_a1  0.6
  mac4_d2  #12
  mac4_a2  0.3
  mac5_d1  #8
  mac5_a1  -0.6
  mac5_d2  #12
  mac5_a2  0.212
  mac6_d1  #13
  mac6_a1  0.4
  mac7_d1  #9
  mac7_a1  0.5
  mac7_d2  #12
  mac7_a2  -0.401
  mac8_d1  #14
  mac8_a1  0.1
  stroke         #3
  body           0.8

